Fourteen

It took 14 full moons
To gather the world's strength
For 14 seconds of conversation.
It was merely an introduction,
Yet it occupied a corner of my heart.

I could never forget the smile you held,
The one that compels me to blush
Every time I think about it,
Even now, as I read it aloud.

I’m still lost in thought,
Why I wrote full 14 pages in my diary
To elaborate on those 14 seconds.

It truly took me 14 full moons.
For the 14 seconds of conversation.
